<!DOCTYPE html><html lang="en"> <head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1"><title>Deck and Fence Staining in Central Massachusetts | MCB</title><meta name="description" content="Deck and fence staining in Central Massachusetts: when new pressure-treated wood is ready, cleaning and stripping, choosing opacity, and typical 2026 costs."><link rel="canonical" href="https://mcitybuilders.com/painting/deck-and-fence-staining"><meta property="og:type" content="website"><meta property="og:title" content="Deck and Fence Staining in Central Massachusetts | MCB"><meta property="og:description" content="Deck and fence staining in Central Massachusetts: when new pressure-treated wood is ready, cleaning and stripping, choosing opacity, and typical 2026 costs."><meta property="og:url" content="https://mcitybuilders.com/painting/deck-and-fence-staining"><meta property="og:site_name" content="Maverick City Builders"><meta name="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image"><link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com"><link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin><link rel="stylesheet" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Manrope:wght@200;300;400;500;600;700&family=IBM+Plex+Mono:wght@400;500&display=swap"><script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"GeneralContractor","@id":"https://mcitybuilders.com/#business","name":"Maverick City Builders","url":"https://mcitybuilders.com","telephone":"(508) 656-7436","email":"douglas@mcitybuilders.com","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","streetAddress":"1171 Main St","addressLocality":"Lancaster","addressRegion":"MA","postalCode":"01523","addressCountry":"US"},"geo":{"@type":"GeoCoordinates","latitude":42.4556,"longitude":-71.6731},"sameAs":["https://www.facebook.com/mcitybuilders","https://www.instagram.com/mcitybuilders"]}</script><script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"BreadcrumbList","itemListElement":[{"@type":"ListItem","position":1,"name":"Home","item":"https://mcitybuilders.com/"},{"@type":"ListItem","position":2,"name":"Painting","item":"https://mcitybuilders.com/painting"},{"@type":"ListItem","position":3,"name":"Deck and fence staining","item":"https://mcitybuilders.com/painting/deck-and-fence-staining"}]}</script><script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Service","serviceType":"Deck and fence staining","url":"https://mcitybuilders.com/painting/deck-and-fence-staining","provider":{"@id":"https://mcitybuilders.com/#business"},"areaServed":{"@type":"AdministrativeArea","name":"Central Massachusetts"}}</script><script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"How long should I wait to stain a new pressure-treated deck?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Until the wood is dry enough to absorb water, not a fixed number of months. Sprinkle water on the boards: if it beads, wait and test again in a few days; if it soaks in, the wood is ready. YellaWood's current guidance is to stain within about six weeks of construction once the wood passes that test."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Semi-transparent or solid stain for a deck floor?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"For walking surfaces, we lean toward transparent or semi-transparent penetrating stains. They soak in and wear away gradually. Solid stains form a film, and on a horizontal deck floor that film tends to peel under foot traffic, snow and standing water. Solid stain works well on railings, fences and vertical boards."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How often does a deck need restaining in Massachusetts?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Horizontal deck boards typically need a maintenance coat every two to three years here; railings and fences last longer because they shed water. Sun, shade and snow load make a big difference, so a south-facing deck usually needs attention sooner than a shaded one."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Do composite or PVC decks need stain?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No. Composite and PVC decking from brands like Trex, TimberTech, AZEK and Fiberon is not stained. It needs washing, and the manufacturer's care instructions should be followed. Only wood parts such as a pressure-treated frame, cedar railings or wood stairs take stain."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can you stain in the fall?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Often into early autumn, if the forecast holds. Stains like Cabot Australian Timber Oil call for air and surface temperatures between 50 and 90°F. Cold nights and heavy morning dew are what end the season in Central Massachusetts, not the calendar."}}]}</script><!-- First-touch attribution. Runs before anything else so a click-id is never
