-astro-cid-nen7h5rs> <a class="hd__tel" href="tel:+15086567436" data-ev="phone_click" data-astro-cid-nen7h5rs>(508) 656-7436</a> <a class="btn hd__cta" href="/contact" data-ev="estimate_cta" data-astro-cid-nen7h5rs>Free estimate</a> <button class="hd__burger" aria-label="Open menu" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="mnav" data-astro-cid-nen7h5rs> <span data-astro-cid-nen7h5rs></span><span data-astro-cid-nen7h5rs></span> </button> </div> </div> <nav class="mnav" id="mnav" hidden aria-label="Mobile" data-astro-cid-nen7h5rs> <div class="wrap" data-astro-cid-nen7h5rs> <a href="/kitchen-remodeling" data-astro-cid-nen7h5rs>Kitchen remodeling</a><a href="/bathroom-remodeling" data-astro-cid-nen7h5rs>Bathroom remodeling</a><a href="/general-renovations" data-astro-cid-nen7h5rs>General renovations</a><a href="/carpentry" data-astro-cid-nen7h5rs>Carpentry</a><a href="/deck-building" data-astro-cid-nen7h5rs>Deck building</a><a href="/interior-painting" data-astro-cid-nen7h5rs>Interior painting</a><a href="/exterior-painting" data-astro-cid-nen7h5rs>Exterior painting</a><a href="/building-restoration" data-astro-cid-nen7h5rs>Building restoration</a><a href="/water-damage-restoration" data-astro-cid-nen7h5rs>Water damage restoration</a> <hr class="rule" data-astro-cid-nen7h5rs> <a href="/painting" data-astro-cid-nen7h5rs>Painting</a><a href="/portfolio" data-astro-cid-nen7h5rs>Our work</a><a href="/areas-we-serve" data-astro-cid-nen7h5rs>Areas we serve</a> <a href="/about" data-astro-cid-nen7h5rs>About</a><a href="/contact" data-astro-cid-nen7h5rs>Free estimate</a> <a class="mnav__tel" href="tel:+15086567436" data-ev="phone_click" data-astro-cid-nen7h5rs>(508) 656-7436</a> </div> </nav> </header> <script type="module">var e=document.querySelector(`.hd__burger`),t=document.getElementById(`mnav`);e?.addEventListener(`click`,()=>{let n=e.getAttribute(`aria-expanded`)===`true`;e.setAttribute(`aria-expanded`,String(!n)),t&&(t.hidden=n),e.setAttribute(`aria-label`,n?`Open menu`:`Close menu`)});</script> <main id="main" data-astro-cid-j5amansv> <section class="top wrap-wide" data-astro-cid-j5amansv> <div data-astro-cid-j5amansv> <nav class="crumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb" data-astro-cid-j5amansv><a href="/" data-astro-cid-j5amansv>Home</a> <span aria-hidden="true" data-astro-cid-j5amansv>/</span> <a href="/painting" data-astro-cid-j5amansv>Painting</a></nav> <h1 data-astro-cid-j5amansv>Deck and fence staining</h1> <p class="cost" data-astro-cid-j5amansv>Typical Central MA range: <strong data-astro-cid-j5amansv>$3–$6 per sq ft of deck; $5–$12 per linear ft of fence (typical Central MA range)</strong></p> <p class="lead" data-astro-cid-j5amansv>Clean, brighten and stain wood decks and fences, with the right opacity and timing for a New England winter.</p> <a class="btn" href="#estimate" data-astro-cid-j5amansv>Book a free in-home consultation</a> </div> <figure data-astro-cid-j5amansv> <img src="/ideas/deck-and-fence-staining-main.webp" alt="Design idea: pressure-treated wood deck with a fresh cedar-tone semi-transparent stain behind a New England colonial, with a matching stained board fence" width="1600" height="1195" fetchpriority="high" data-astro-cid-j5amansv> <figcaption data-astro-cid-j5amansv>Design idea (AI illustration) — not an MCB project photo.</figcaption> </figure> </section> <article class="wrap prose" data-astro-cid-j5amansv> <h2 id="stain-is-maintenance-not-a-one-time-finish">Stain is maintenance, not a one-time finish</h2>
<p>Paint on a house can go seven to ten years. Stain on a deck floor does not come close. A deck in Central Massachusetts takes direct sun all summer, holds snow for weeks, gets shoveled, gets salted near the door, and sits under wet leaves every fall. The walking surface wears first. Railings and fences, which shed water, last longer.</p>
<p>That is why deck and fence staining is really about three decisions: when the wood is ready, how it gets cleaned, and which product and opacity it gets. Get those right and a maintenance coat every few years keeps the wood sound. Get them wrong and you end up paying to strip peeling stain off the boards.</p>
<p>This page covers staining existing wood decks, new pressure-treated decks and wood fences. If you are building or replacing a deck, start with <a href="/deck-building">deck building</a> or <a href="/composite-deck-installers-central-ma">composite decking</a>. For siding and trim, see <a href="/exterior-painting">exterior painting</a>; for a front door in a gloss enamel, see <a href="/painting/trim-door-and-stair-painting">trim, door and stair painting</a>.</p>
<h2 id="who-it-is-right-for-and-where-stain-will-not-help">Who it is right for, and where stain will not help</h2>
<p>Staining is right for pressure-treated pine, cedar and other wood decks, railings, stairs, pergolas and fences that are structurally sound.</p>
<p>It will not help when:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Boards are soft, split or cupped badly.</strong> Stain does not fix rot. Replace damaged boards first, and check the framing under them.</li>
<li><strong>Railings are loose.</strong> Loose posts and balusters are a safety problem to fix before any finish goes on.</li>
<li><strong>The deck is composite or PVC.</strong> Those boards are not stained. Brands like Trex, TimberTech, AZEK and Fiberon are cleaned according to the manufacturer’s instructions instead.</li>
</ul>
<h2 id="what-it-costs-in-central-ma">What it costs in Central MA</h2>
<p>Typical 2026 ranges, not quotes. The written estimate itemises cleaning, stripping, board replacement, the named stain and coat count, and anything excluded.</p>
<table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Typical scope</th>
<th>Typical Central MA range</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td>New pressure-treated deck about 12 x 16 ft, cleaned and one coat semi-transparent</td>
<td>$700–$1,300</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Existing deck, washed, brightened and re-coated</td>
<td>$3–$5 per sq ft</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Failed film stain stripped, sanded and re-stained</td>
<td>$5–$9 per sq ft</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Railings and balusters</td>
<td>$6–$14 per linear ft of railing</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Wood fence, one side</td>
<td>$5–$12 per linear ft</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Deck boards replaced before staining</td>
<td>Priced per board after inspection</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<p>Stripping is what drives the price up. A deck that was coated with solid stain or deck paint and is now peeling takes far more labor than one that was kept up with a penetrating stain.</p>
<h2 id="how-the-job-runs-step-by-step">How the job runs, step by step</h2>
<p>A typical scope looks like this:</p>
<ol>
<li><strong>Inspect.</strong> Walk the deck, check for soft boards, loose railings and popped fasteners, and test how the wood absorbs water.</li>
<li><strong>Protect.</strong> Plants, siding and the house foundation get covered or wetted before any cleaner goes on.</li>
<li><strong>Clean or strip.</strong> Weathered wood gets a wood cleaner to lift gray fibers and mildew. Failed film stain gets a stripper. Pressure washing is done at low pressure with a fan tip; high pressure furs the wood and gouges soft pine.</li>
<li><strong>Brighten.</strong> A wood brightener after cleaning or stripping restores the wood’s color and helps stain soak in evenly.</li>
<li><strong>Dry and sand.</strong> The wood dries for a few days. Raised grain and fuzzed fibers get sanded.</li>
<li><strong>Stain.</strong> Applied by brush, pad or sprayer and back-brushed, following the manufacturer’s coverage. Many penetrating stains are one coat; over-applying leaves a sticky surface that wears badly.</li>
<li><strong>Cure.</strong> Stay off the deck for the time listed on the can, usually a day or two, and keep furniture off longer.</li>
</ol>
<p>Timeline: most decks take two to four days from cleaning to final coat, mostly drying time. Fences depend on length and whether both sides are done.</p>
<h2 id="choosing-the-stain">Choosing the stain</h2>
<p>Opacity is the main choice:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Transparent and semi-transparent</strong> stains soak into the wood, show the grain and wear away instead of peeling. They are the safer choice for deck floors.</li>
<li><strong>Semi-solid and solid</strong> stains hide the grain and look closer to paint. They are best on railings, fences and vertical boards, and on older wood with mismatched repairs.</li>
</ul>
<p>The products we use:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Cabot Australian Timber Oil.</strong> An oil-based, penetrating stain for decks and outdoor wood that shows the grain, applied as one coat. Cabot also makes Wood Cleaner and Wood Brightener for prep.</li>
<li><strong>Cabot Semi-Transparent and Solid Color stains.</strong> For fences and railings, Cabot has oil and water-based options across every opacity, including Solid Color Acrylic Stain + Sealer.</li>
<li><strong>ProLuxe (formerly Sikkens) SRD.</strong> A one-coat, penetrating transparent wood finish for decks, railings and siding, tinted with high-transparency pigments so the grain shows through. ProLuxe also makes a dedicated deck finish, formerly sold as Cetol DEK.</li>
</ul>
<p>Manufacturer warranties vary by product and require installation to the manufacturer’s instructions, so we follow the label on prep, temperature and coverage.</p>
<h2 id="new-england-issues">New England issues</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>New pressure-treated lumber.</strong> Fresh lumber is often too wet to stain. Use the sprinkle test: water that beads means wait; water that soaks in means the wood is ready.</li>
<li><strong>Temperature and dew.</strong> Cabot lists 50 to 90°F for air and surface temperature on Australian Timber Oil. Late-day stain in September can be ruined by overnight dew before it soaks in.</li>
<li><strong>Snow, shovels and ice melt.</strong> Metal shovels scrape stain off the boards, and ice melt near the back door wears the finish. Use a plastic shovel and a product the decking manufacturer allows.</li>
<li><strong>Shade and mildew.</strong> North-facing decks and fences under trees in Bolton, Harvard and Westford lots grow mildew fast. They need regular cleaning more than extra stain.</li>
<li><strong>Older painted porches.</strong> Scraping painted porch floors or railings on a pre-1978 house in Lancaster or Concord can disturb lead paint, and that work falls under EPA RRP and Massachusetts lead-safe rules. Ask any contractor for their Massachusetts lead-safe renovation credentials in writing before work that disturbs paint in a pre-1978 home.</li>
</ul>
<h2 id="what-to-ask-any-contractor">What to ask any contractor</h2>
<ul>
<li>Which stain, by name and opacity, and how many coats?</li>
<li>Will you clean, brighten, or strip, and why?</li>
<li>What pressure and tip will you use on the wood?</li>
<li>How will you protect plants, siding and the foundation?</li>
<li>How soon can we use the deck, and when should it be recoated?</li>
</ul>
<p>For a firm number, book a free in-home consultation. We inspect the boards and railings, test how the wood takes water, show stain samples on your own wood, and send a written estimate that spells out prep, product and coats.</p>
 <section class="faq" data-astro-cid-j5amansv> <h2 data-astro-cid-j5amansv>Common questions</h2> <details data-astro-cid-j5amansv><summary data-astro-cid-j5amansv>How long should I wait to stain a new pressure-treated deck?</summary><p data-astro-cid-j5amansv>Until the wood is dry enough to absorb water, not a fixed number of months. Sprinkle water on the boards: if it beads, wait and test again in a few days; if it soaks in, the wood is ready. YellaWood&#39;s current guidance is to stain within about six weeks of construction once the wood passes that test.</p></details><details data-astro-cid-j5amansv><summary data-astro-cid-j5amansv>Semi-transparent or solid stain for a deck floor?</summary><p data-astro-cid-j5amansv>For walking surfaces, we lean toward transparent or semi-transparent penetrating stains. They soak in and wear away gradually. Solid stains form a film, and on a horizontal deck floor that film tends to peel under foot traffic, snow and standing water. Solid stain works well on railings, fences and vertical boards.</p></details><details data-astro-cid-j5amansv><summary data-astro-cid-j5amansv>How often does a deck need restaining in Massachusetts?</summary><p data-astro-cid-j5amansv>Horizontal deck boards typically need a maintenance coat every two to three years here; railings and fences last longer because they shed water. Sun, shade and snow load make a big difference, so a south-facing deck usually needs attention sooner than a shaded one.</p></details><details data-astro-cid-j5amansv><summary data-astro-cid-j5amansv>Do composite or PVC decks need stain?</summary><p data-astro-cid-j5amansv>No. Composite and PVC decking from brands like Trex, TimberTech, AZEK and Fiberon is not stained. It needs washing, and the manufacturer&#39;s care instructions should be followed. Only wood parts such as a pressure-treated frame, cedar railings or wood stairs take stain.</p></details><details data-astro-cid-j5amansv><summary data-astro-cid-j5amansv>Can you stain in the fall?</summary><p data-astro-cid-j5amansv>Often into early autumn, if the forecast holds. Stains like Cabot Australian Timber Oil call for air and surface temperatures between 50 and 90°F. Cold nights and heavy morning dew are what end the season in Central Massachusetts, not the calendar.</p></details> </section> </article> <section class="wrap-wide more" data-astro-cid-j5amansv> <h2 data-astro-cid-j5amansv>More painting ideas</h2> <ul data-astro-cid-j5amansv> <li data-astro-cid-j5amansv><a href="/painting/trim-door-and-stair-painting" data-astro-cid-j5amansv><img src="/ideas/trim-door-and-stair-painting-detail.webp" alt="Design idea: close-up of a brushed semi-gloss enamel finish on a six-panel door" width="800" height="800" loading="lazy" data-astro-cid-j5amansv><span data-astro-cid-j5amansv>Trim, door and stair painting</span></a></li><li data-astro-cid-j5amansv><a href="/painting/drywall-repair-and-painting" data-astro-cid-j5amansv><img src="/ideas/drywall-repair-and-painting-detail.webp" alt="Design idea: close-up of a feathered joint compound patch on drywall ready for primer" width="800" height="800" loading="lazy" data-astro-cid-j5amansv><span data-astro-cid-j5amansv>Drywall repair and painting</span></a></li><li data-astro-cid-j5amansv><a href="/painting/wallpaper-removal" data-astro-cid-j5amansv><img src="/ideas/wallpaper-removal-detail.webp" alt="Design idea: close-up of a strip of old patterned wallpaper peeling back from a plaster wall" width="800" height="800" loading="lazy" data-astro-cid-j5amansv><span data-astro-cid-j5amansv>Wallpaper removal</span></a></li> </ul> <p data-astro-cid-j5amansv><a href="/painting" data-astro-cid-j5amansv>Back to painting</a></p> </section> <div id="estimate" data-astro-cid-j5amansv><form class="ef" id="estimate-form" novalidate data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn> <div class="ef__row" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn> <label for="ef-name" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>Name <abbr title="required" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>*</abbr></label> <input id="ef-name" name="name" type="text" autocomplete="name" required data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn> <p class="ef__err" data-err="ef-name" hidden data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>Please tell us your name.</p> </div> <div class="ef__grid" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn> <div class="ef__row" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn> <label for="ef-phone" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>Phone <abbr title="required" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>*</abbr></label> <input id="ef-phone" name="phone" type="tel" inputmode="tel" autocomplete="tel" required data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn> <p class="ef__err" data-err="ef-phone" hidden data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>We need a phone number to reach you.</p> </div> <div class="ef__row" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn> <label for="ef-email" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>Email</label> <input id="ef-email" name="email" type="email" inputmode="email" autocomplete="email" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn> <p class="ef__err" data-err="ef-email" hidden data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>That email address doesn't look right.</p> </div> </div> <div class="ef__grid" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn> <div class="ef__row" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn> <label for="ef-town" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>Project town <abbr title="required" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>*</abbr></label> <input id="ef-town" name="town" type="text" autocomplete="address-level2" required data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn> <p class="ef__err" data-err="ef-town" hidden data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>Which town is the project in?</p> </div> <div class="ef__row" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn> <label for="ef-type" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>Project type <abbr title="required" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>*</abbr></label> <select id="ef-type" name="projectType" required data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn> <option value="" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>Choose one…</option> <option value="Kitchen remodeling" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>Kitchen remodeling</option><option value="Bathroom remodeling" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>Bathroom remodeling</option><option value="General renovations" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>General renovations</option><option value="Carpentry" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>Carpentry</option><option value="Deck building" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>Deck building</option><option value="Interior painting" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>Interior painting</option><option value="Exterior painting" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>Exterior painting</option><option value="Building restoration" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>Building restoration</option><option value="Water damage restoration" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>Water damage restoration</option> <option value="Multiple / not sure" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>Multiple, or not sure yet</option> </select> <p class="ef__err" data-err="ef-type" hidden data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>Please pick the closest match.</p> </div> </div> <div class="ef__row" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn> <label for="ef-details" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>Project details <abbr title="required" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>*</abbr></label> <textarea id="ef-details" name="projectDetails" rows="5" required placeholder="What you want done, roughly when, and anything you already know about the space." data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn></textarea> <p class="ef__err" data-err="ef-details" hidden data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>A sentence or two is plenty.</p> </div> <div class="ef__grid" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn> <div class="ef__row" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn> <label for="ef-timing" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>Desired timing</label> <select id="ef-timing" name="timing" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn> <option value="" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>No strong preference</option> <option data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>As soon as possible</option><option data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>Within 1–3 months</option> <option data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>Within 3–6 months</option><option data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>Later this year</option> <option data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>Just planning / budgeting</option> </select> </div> <div class="ef__row" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn> <label for="ef-contact" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>Preferred contact</label> <select id="ef-contact" name="preferredContact" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn> <option data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>Phone call</option><option data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>Text message</option><option data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>Email</option> </select> </div> </div> <!-- Honeypot. Off-screen, aria-hidden, never focusable. --> <div class="ef__hp" aria-hidden="true" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn> <label for="ef-company" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>Company</label> <input id="ef-company" name="company" type="text" tabindex="-1" autocomplete="off" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn> </div> <p class="ef__consent" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>
By sending this you agree we can contact you about your project by phone, text or email.
    Message rates may apply. Reply STOP to opt out of texts at any time. We don't sell your details.
</p> <button class="btn ef__submit" type="submit" data-ev="form_submit" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>Send it over</button> <p class="ef__note" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>We read every one of these. Prefer to talk?
<a href="tel:+15086567436" data-ev="phone_click" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>(508) 656-7436</a>.</p> <p class="ef__fail" id="ef-fail" role="alert" hidden data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn></p> </form> <div class="ef__ok" id="ef-ok" role="status" hidden data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn> <h3 data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>Got it.</h3> <p data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>Your details are with us. We'll be in touch to arrange a look at the project.
     If it's urgent, call <a href="tel:+15086567436" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>(508) 656-7436</a>.</p> </div> <script>(function(){const CRM = {"endpoint":"https://backend.leadconnectorhq.com/external-tracking/events","locationId":"b5lmCvdlpVkhC4JOVBjd","trackingId":"tk_e76468050a3e42e0b65b2fa5b3c87a7f"};
const PHONE = "(508) 656-7436";
const EMAIL = "douglas@mcitybuilders.com";

  const form = document.getElementById('estimate-form');
  const okBox = document.getElementById('ef-ok');
  const failBox = document.getElementById('ef-fail');
  if (form) {
    const started = Date.now();
    let announcedStart = false;
    form.addEventListener('input', () => {
      if (!announcedStart && typeof gtag === 'function') {
        announcedStart = true;
        gtag('event', 'form_start', { form_id: 'mcb_estimate' });   // no field contents
      }
    }, { once: false });

    const showErr = (el, on) => {
      el.setAttribute('aria-invalid', String(on));
      const p = form.querySelector('[data-err="' + el.id + '"]');
      if (p) p.hidden = !on;
    };

    form.addEventListener('submit', async (e) => {
      e.preventDefault();
      failBox.hidden = true;

      // --- validation with real messages, focus moved to the first problem
      let firstBad = null;
      for (const el of form.querySelectorAll('[required]')) {
        const bad = !el.value.trim();
        showErr(el, bad);
        if (bad && !firstBad) firstBad = el;
      }
      const em = form.querySelector('#ef-email');
      const emBad = em.value.trim() !== '' && !/^[^@\s]+@[^@\s]+\.[^@\s]{2,}$/.test(em.value.trim());
      showErr(em, emBad);
      if (emBad && !firstBad) firstBad = em;
      if (firstBad) { firstBad.focus(); return; }

      // --- bot gates: hidden field filled, or submitted faster than a human types
      const fd = new FormData(form);
      if (String(fd.get('company') || '').trim() !== '' || Date.now() - started < 3000) {
        form.hidden = true; okBox.hidden = false; return;   // silent, nothing sent
      }

      const btn = form.querySelector('.ef__submit');
      const label = btn.textContent;
      btn.textContent = 'Sending…'; btn.disabled = true;

      let ss = null; try { ss = sessionStorage; } catch (_) {}
      const attr = (k) => { try { return (ss && ss.getItem('mcb_' + k)) || ''; } catch (_) { return ''; } };

      const payload = {
        type: 'external_form_submission',
        timestamp: Date.now(),
        formId: 'Estimate Request',
        formData: {
          full_name: fd.get('name'),
          phone: fd.get('phone'),
          email: fd.get('email') || '',          // logical OR. Not a pipe.
          'contact.project_details': fd.get('projectDetails'),
          project_town: fd.get('town'),
          project_type: fd.get('projectType'),
          timing: fd.get('timing') || '',
          preferred_contact: fd.get('preferredContact') || '',
          utm_source: attr('utm_source'), utm_medium: attr('utm_medium'),
          utm_campaign: attr('utm_campaign'), utm_term: attr('utm_term'),
          utm_content: attr('utm_content'), gclid: attr('gclid'), fbclid: attr('fbclid'),
          landing_page: attr('mcb_landing') || attr('landing'),
          referrer: attr('referrer') || document.referrer || '',
          Timezone: Intl.DateTimeFormat().resolvedOptions().timeZone,
        },
        url: location.href, title: document.title, path: location.pathname,
        userAgent: navigator.userAgent,
        trackingId: CRM.trackingId, locationId: CRM.locationId,
        sessionId: (crypto && crypto.randomUUID) ? crypto.randomUUID() : String(Math.random()).slice(2),
      };

      let ok = false, diag = '';
      try {
        const res = await fetch(CRM.endpoint, {
          method: 'POST',
          headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json', version: '2021-07-28' },
          body: JSON.stringify(payload),
        });
        ok = res.ok; diag = 'HTTP ' + res.status;
      } catch (err) { diag = 'network: ' + (err && err.message); }

      if (!ok) {
        // Nothing reached the CRM. Keep every keystroke on screen, give a real
        // route through, and do NOT report a conversion.
        console.error('[MCB estimate form]', diag);
        btn.textContent = label; btn.disabled = false;
        failBox.innerHTML = 'We couldn\'t send that from the website. Please call ' +
          '<a href="tel:+15086567436">' + PHONE + '</a> or email ' +
          '<a href="mailto:' + EMAIL + '">' + EMAIL + '</a>. ' +
          'Everything you typed is still in the form above.';
        failBox.hidden = false;
        failBox.scrollIntoView({ behavior: 'smooth', block: 'center' });
        return;
      }

      if (typeof gtag === 'function') {
        gtag('event', 'generate_lead', { form_id: 'mcb_estimate', lead_source: 'website_estimate_form' });
      }
      form.hidden = true; okBox.hidden = false;
      okBox.scrollIntoView({ behavior: 'smooth', block: 'center' });
      okBox.querySelector('h3').setAttribute('tabindex', '-1');
      okBox.querySelector('h3').focus();
    });
  }
})();</script></div> </main> <footer class="ft" data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk> <div class="wrap" data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk> <div class="ft__top" data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk> <div data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk> <span class="eyebrow" data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk>Maverick City Builders</span> <p class="ft__pitch" data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk>General contracting and remodeling across Massachusetts.</p> <a class="btn btn--onDark" href="/contact" data-ev="estimate_cta" data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk>Request an estimate</a> </div> <nav aria-label="Services" data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk><h2 class="ft__h" data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk>Services</h2> <ul data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk><li data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk><a href="/kitchen-remodeling" data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk>Kitchen remodeling</a></li><li data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk><a href="/bathroom-remodeling" data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk>Bathroom remodeling</a></li><li data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk><a href="/general-renovations" data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk>General renovations</a></li><li data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk><a href="/carpentry" data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk>Carpentry</a></li><li data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk><a href="/deck-building" data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk>Deck building</a></li><li data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk><a href="/interior-painting" data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk>Interior painting</a></li><li data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk><a href="/exterior-painting" data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk>Exterior painting</a></li><li data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk><a href="/building-restoration" data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk>Building restoration</a></li><li data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk><a href="/water-damage-restoration" data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk>Water damage restoration</a></li></ul> </nav> <nav aria-label="Company" data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk><h2 class="ft__h" data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk>Company</h2> <ul data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk> <li data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk><a href="/about" data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk>About</a></li><li data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk><a href="/portfolio" data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk>Our work</a></li> <li data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk><a href="/areas-we-serve" data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk>Areas we serve</a></li><li data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk><a href="/blog" data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk>Articles</a></li> <li data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk><a href="/contact" data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk>Contact</a></li> </ul> </nav> <div data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk><h2 class="ft__h" data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk>Contact</h2> <address class="ft__nap" data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk> <a href="tel:+15086567436" data-ev="phone_click" data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk>(508) 656-7436</a> <a href="mailto:douglas@mcitybuilders.com" data-ev="email_click" data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk>douglas@mcitybuilders.com</a> <span data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk>1171 Main St<br data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk>Lancaster, MA 01523</span> <em data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk>Office visits by appointment</em> </address> </div> </div> <hr class="rule" data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk> <div class="ft__base" data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk> <p data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk>&copy; 2026 Maverick City Builders &middot; Lancaster, Massachusetts</p> <p data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk><a href="/privacy-policy" data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk>Privacy</a> &middot; <a href="/terms" data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk>Terms</a> &middot;
<a href="/accessibility" data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk>Accessibility</a> &middot; <a href="/cookie-policy" data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk>Cookies</a></p> </div> </div> </footer> </main>  <div id="mcb-cookie-banner" hidden role="dialog" aria-live="polite" aria-label="Cookie choices" style="position:fixed;left:0;right:0;bottom:0;z-index:99999;background:#0b0b0b;border-top:2px solid #E10600;color:#e6e6e6;padding:18px 20px;font-size:14px;line-height:1.55;display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:14px;align-items:center;justify-content:center"> <span style="max-width:640px">We measure page views with Google Analytics in cookieless mode. Accept to allow analytics cookies and ad measurement; Decline to stay cookieless. Read our <a href="/cookie-policy" style="color:#ff6b6b;text-decoration:underline">Cookie Policy</a>.</span> <span style="display:flex;gap:10px"> <button type="button" id="mcb-cookie-decline" style="background:transparent;color:#e6e6e6;border:1px solid #777;padding:12px 20px;min-height:44px;border-radius:4px;font-weight:600;cursor:pointer;font-size:13px">Decline</button> <button type="button" id="mcb-cookie-accept" style="background:#E10600;color:#fff;border:0;padding:12px 22px;min-height:44px;border-radius:4px;font-weight:700;cursor:pointer;font-size:13px">Accept</button> </span> </div> <!-- Analytics with Google Consent Mode (mcb-consent-v2, 2026-09-18, Doug's decision).
       GA4 loads by default with analytics_storage DENIED = cookieless pings, no _ga cookie.
       Accept upgrades consent to granted. Browsers sending Do-Not-Track or Global Privacy
       Control get nothing at all. The static site does the same via patch_consent.py. --> <script>(function(){const ga4 = "G-7HXJQJL5Q2";

    (function () {
      var KEY = 'mcb-consent'; // MUST match the static site's key (hyphen). An underscore here meant GA4 never loaded on any Astro page.
      var dnt = false;
      try { dnt = navigator.doNotTrack == '1' || window.doNotTrack == '1' || !!navigator.globalPrivacyControl; } catch (e) {}
      window.dataLayer = window.dataLayer || [];
      window.gtag = function () { window.dataLayer.push(arguments); };
      gtag('consent', 'default', { ad_storage: 'denied', ad_user_data: 'denied', ad_personalization: 'denied',
        analytics_storage: 'denied', functionality_storage: 'granted', security_storage: 'granted' });
      function load() {
        if (window.__mcbTagged) return; window.__mcbTagged = true;
        var s = document.createElement('script'); s.async = true;
        s.src = 'https://www.googletagmanager.com/gtag/js?id=' + ga4;
        document.head.appendChild(s);
        gtag('js', new Date()); gtag('config', ga4);
      }
      function boot() { // Accept: cookies + ad measurement allowed
        gtag('consent', 'update', { ad_storage: 'granted', ad_user_data: 'granted', ad_personalization: 'granted', analytics_storage: 'granted' });
        load();
      }
      var stored = null;
      try { stored = localStorage.getItem(KEY); } catch (e) {}
      if (stored === 'granted') boot();
      else if (!dnt) load(); // undecided or declined: cookieless measurement only
      window.__mcbConsentBoot = boot;
      // Same banner as the static site. Without it a visitor who LANDS on a town page
      // is never asked, so is never measured.
      try {
        var v = localStorage.getItem(KEY), b = document.getElementById('mcb-cookie-banner');
        if (b && v !== 'granted' && v !== 'denied') {
          b.hidden = false;
          document.getElementById('mcb-cookie-accept').addEventListener('click', function () { try { localStorage.setItem(KEY, 'granted'); } catch (e) {} b.hidden = true; boot(); });
          document.getElementById('mcb-cookie-decline').addEventListener('click', function () { try { localStorage.setItem(KEY, 'denied'); } catch (e) {} b.hidden = true; });
        }
      } catch (e) {}
      // lightweight, non-sensitive interaction events
      document.addEventListener('click', function (e) {
        var a = e.target && e.target.closest && e.target.closest('[data-ev]');
        if (a && typeof window.gtag === 'function') {
          gtag('event', a.getAttribute('data-ev'), { link_url: a.getAttribute('href') || '' });
        }
      }, true);
    })();
  })();</script></body> </html>